I could not derive this rigorously. The answer below is a guess based on recollection of the relevant literature (Bader–Fisher–Miller–Stover-type rigidity results for lattices in $\operatorname{SO}(n,1)\subset\operatorname{SO}(n,2)$), not a verified computation.

The setup is that $G_n=\operatorname{SO}(n,2)_0$ and $H_n=\operatorname{SO}(n,1)_0$, with $\Gamma$ a cocompact lattice in $H_n$ and $\rho_j$ a sequence of deformations converging to the inclusion. The existence of such deformations with Zariski dense, infinite-covolume, ergodic images is the kind of phenomenon these rigidity results constrain. I believe the threshold falls at $n=4$, but I have not verified this.

